  Option 1: Gradio (easiest migration, ~1 day)                                                                  
                                                                   
  Built specifically for ML apps. No full-script reruns, streaming predictions, and real-time training progress 
  are first-class features.                                                                                   
                                                                                                                
  Best fit for TargetTrace because:                         
  - gr.Progress() replaces the threading hack for training updates
  - Tabbed layout maps 1:1 to your current pages                                                                
  - gr.Dataframe, gr.Plot handle batch prediction and charts natively
  - Inference streaming via yield                                                                               
                                                                                                                
  import gradio as gr                                                                                           
                                                                                                                
  def predict(smiles, sequence):                                                                                
      results = _predict(smiles, sequence)
      return pd.DataFrame(results)                                                                              
                                                            
  def train_model(epochs, progress=gr.Progress()):                                                              
      for ep, total, loss, acc, mae in _train_generator(epochs):
          progress(ep / total, desc=f"Epoch {ep}/{total} — loss {loss:.3f}")                                    
      return "Done"                                                                                             
                                                                                                                
  with gr.Blocks() as app:                                                                                      
      with gr.Tab("Predict"):                                                                                   
          smiles_in = gr.Textbox(label="SMILES")            
          seq_in    = gr.Textbox(label="Protein sequence (optional)")                                           
          out_table = gr.Dataframe()                                                                            
          gr.Button("Predict").click(predict, [smiles_in, seq_in], out_table)                                   
      with gr.Tab("Train"):                                                                                     
          epochs = gr.Slider(5, 50, value=10)               
          gr.Button("Train").click(train_model, epochs, gr.Textbox())                                           
                                                                                                                
  Tradeoff: Less flexible layout than Streamlit. Not great for complex multi-column dashboards.  
